From e093e37bebb2bf25410675353056721c6943177b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:07:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cli: the reader's notes on stderr, --algorithm for nest

From the review on the pull request: a script could not tell a clean
read from one where the reader had to leave something out, and the
nesting could not be asked for the other algorithm.

What the reader had to do to open the file (Opened::notes: a texture
missing from it, an object rebuilt from geometry.glb, plugin data that
is not text) now goes to stderr, one "sawhorse-cli: note: ..." line
each, before the JSON on stdout, so stdout stays parseable. run()
returns Printed { text, notes }; open(), cut_list_text() and
nest_text() take an opened file so it is read once.

nest takes --algorithm guillotine|maxrects (table-saw and cnc as
aliases); unset, the document's own, as before. cutlist refuses it.

Tests: cutlist.rs (both algorithms reach the kernel and the JSON says
which; a saved file rewritten with a plugin-data.json that is not text
comes back with the reader's note and the same cut list, a clean file
with none; the new options and refusals on the command line).

