 ### Added (a headless cut list, 2026-11-05)
 
-- **`sawhorse-cli`: the cut list or the nesting of a saved `.shz` as JSON, with no app** ([#14](https://github.com/sawhorse3d/sawhorse/issues/14): "reading a cut list from a .shz as JSON without opening the app"). `sawhorse-cli cutlist Bookshelf.shz` prints what the Cut list pane reads (rows with finished sizes, quantities, grain, stock, board feet or area, the totals, the hash), `sawhorse-cli nest Bookshelf.shz` what the Nesting section reads; `--visible-only`, `--rounding sixteenth|thirty-second|half-mm` (cutlist) and `--pretty`. It is the kernel's own serialization through `sawhorse_shz::read`, so a file gives the same JSON here and in the app. A new workspace crate, `crates/cli`, with no dependency beyond the kernel, the reader and serde_json; it reads and prints, never writes. A CLI that builds or changes a model, and an MCP server, are not in this; the kernel's op log makes both possible later.
